  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The East Nusa Tenggara Regional Police (Polda NTT) have upgraded the legal status of the rape allegations involving Kupang Regent Yosef Lede to a full investigation. This move follows extensive evidence collection and witness testimonies. To date, investigators have examined 13 witnesses, including the individual who allegedly brought the victim to the regent's house. Police have also confiscated three items as evidence, which include personal clothing items belonging to the victim. The case has drawn national attention, with government officials, including Deputy Minister Veronica Tan, issuing public responses regarding the seriousness of the allegations. The investigation remains active as authorities prepare to question the regent. The case centers on reported events occurring at the official residence of the Kupang Regent, sparking widespread concern and scrutiny from law enforcement and the public.",
